# iOS · Swift Package AppsideSDK

Swift package with a main-actor API. The Safari presenter uses modern Swift concurrency annotations (Xcode 16+). All eight XCTest cases pass on macOS. iOS simulator SDK typecheck also passes in Swift 6 mode for the UIKit/Safari presenter; this is compile validation, not a UI interaction test.

```swift
import AppsideSDK
let sdk = Appside(baseURL: URL(string: "https://your-studio-host")!,
                  openURL: { url in browser.open(url) },
                  closeURL: { browser.dismiss() })
browser.onStoreClosed = { [weak sdk] in sdk?.browserClosed() }
try sdk.configure("orbit", environment: "test", returnURL: URL(string: "orbit://return")!)
try await sdk.openStore(playerToken)
try await sdk.purchase("voyager", playerToken: freshPlayerToken)
let result = try sdk.handle(incomingURL)
```

Retain the Appside instance and an `AppsideBrowser(presenter:)` on iOS. Wire the browser’s `onStoreClosed` to `sdk.browserClosed()` as above; attach application close UI handling to `sdk.onStoreClosed`. Core network/openURL transport is injectable for tests. Call SDK methods and handle returns serially (normally main actor). Forward SwiftUI `onOpenURL` or UIApplication link callbacks into `handle`; associated domain setup belongs to the host app.

All purchases are TEST only. `PurchaseResult` (`status`, `orderId`, `state`, `verified=false`) is a UI hint; grant items only on your backend using verified webhooks or authenticated `getOrder`. Callback names: `onPurchaseCompleted`, `onPurchaseCanceled`, `onPurchaseFailed`, `onStoreClosed`. A successful launch is not a completed purchase.

Register the exact `returnURL` in Studio → Integration, configure your app's link handler, and pass incoming URLs to `handle`. Each launch needs a fresh backend-issued player token. The SDK correlates returns with pending launch state and rejects replay. Native pending state is in memory: after process death, reopen with a fresh token.

CLT fallback command: `swiftc Sources/AppsideSDK/Appside.swift Smoke/Main.swift -o /tmp/appside-smoke && /tmp/appside-smoke` (run from this directory).

Only one launch is permitted at a time, including while the network request is pending. Concurrent attempts throw `storeAlreadyOpen`. `isStoreOpen` reflects the pending/open session. Safari Done calls `browserClosed()`, invalidates all pending return state and prevents a late launch response opening another browser. A validated callback invokes `closeURL` before the purchase result callback. Invalid callbacks do not dismiss an active session. Reconfiguration while active is rejected.

Launch responses must contain an absolute HTTP(S) URL with a host (HTTP remains supported for local development). Task cancellation is checked before launch and after transport returns, so a canceled task cannot open a late response even when a custom transport ignores cancellation.

