# Node server SDK

Node 20+ ESM. Tests executed with `npm test --prefix sdks/node`. Backend only; never bundle private keys or server keys in clients.

```js
import {Appside} from './sdks/node/index.js';
const appside = new Appside({storeId:'orbit', issuer:'orbit', kid:'key-1',
  privateKey: pemOrKeyObject, webhookSecret: process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET,
  serverKey: process.env.APPSIDE_SERVER_KEY, baseURL:'https://your-studio-host'});
const token = appside.playerToken(authenticatedPlayerId);
const valid = appside.verifyWebhook(rawBodyBuffer, request.headers);
const order = await appside.getOrder(orderId);
```

`playerToken` returns ES256 JWS using P-256 and a fresh nonce, 300-second expiry. Upload the matching public JWK and kid to Integration. `verifyWebhook` returns boolean using raw bytes and header object/Headers; rejects stale signatures. `getOrder` returns Promise<order> and throws on HTTP error; it includes the tenant-bound server bearer key and a 10-second timeout. Grant/dedupe on your server, never from a client result.

Since 0.1.1, `playerToken(playerId, attributes)` optionally signs trusted backend targeting data: `level` (integer 0–1,000,000), `spenderTier` (`none`, `low`, `medium`, `high`), `country` (two uppercase ASCII letters), and `newPlayer` (boolean). All fields are optional; invalid values throw and unknown fields are discarded. Omitting attributes keeps the existing token format. See https://appside.build/docs/player-tokens/ for examples.
